From: plastron
Subject: [PATCH] devfreq: px30_dmc: keep the DDR at the loader's rate at probe

The driver started on simple_ondemand, whose first look, 50 ms after the
probe, read the low bus load of a system still booting and moved the DDR
from the 1056 MHz U-Boot's FSP_INIT leaves it at down to 328 MHz, about
0.46 s into the kernel. The card's UHS-I tuning and the root's first
reads were in flight then, and init's datapart, which sets the
performance governor, moved it back up a moment later. Neither the
launcher's idle ceiling nor steady-memory comes in until seconds after.

Some GKD Pixel 2s crashed on cold starts exactly in that window, 0.13 to
0.38 s after the probe that succeeded, before init ran or just after:
paging requests at fffffefffffffff0 and fffefefffffffff0 in
insert_vmap_area (a vmap tree pointer with bits flipped), one in
terminate_walk and an init killed by SIGSEGV on 1.0.6 (pstore,
2026-11-21 to 26).

Start on performance instead when the loader's rate is the table's top
step: it asks for the rate the DDR already runs at, px30_dmc_target()
returns at once, and nothing switches. It is the governor init sets
anyway, so the launcher's and Diatom's ceilings (max_freq) work as
before and simple_ondemand stays one write away. Any other boot rate is
held as it is, under userspace. The probe says which, with the rate.
---
--- a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
@@ -340,7 +340,8 @@
 	struct arm_smccc_res res;
 	struct dev_pm_opp *opp;
 	struct px30_dmc *dmc;
-	unsigned long freq;
+	unsigned long freq, max;
+	const char *gov;
 	int irq, ret;
 
 	res = px30_dmc_sip(0, PX30_DRAM_GET_VERSION);
@@ -430,8 +431,35 @@
 		.initial_freq	= freq,
 	};
 
-	dmc->devfreq = devm_devfreq_add_device(dev, &dmc->profile,
-					       DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND,
+	/*
+	 * No switch at probe: the DDR stays at the rate the loader left it
+	 * at until user space asks for another. simple_ondemand's first look,
+	 * 50 ms after this, read a booting system's low bus load and moved the
+	 * DDR from 1056 to 328 MHz about 0.46 s into the kernel, with the
+	 * card's UHS-I tuning and the root's first reads in flight; init's
+	 * performance (datapart) moved it back up a moment later. Some GKD
+	 * Pixel 2s crashed on cold starts right there, before init or just
+	 * after it, on corrupted kernel pointers (2026-11-21 to 26).
+	 *
+	 * performance when the loader's rate is the top step: the rate it asks
+	 * for is the one the DDR already runs at, so px30_dmc_target() returns
+	 * at once, and it is the governor init sets anyway, so the system's
+	 * own ceilings (max_freq: the launcher's idle one, a game's) work as
+	 * before. Any other rate (the loader's training did not run, another
+	 * DDR type) is held as it is, under userspace. simple_ondemand stays
+	 * one write away, with its thresholds above.
+	 */
+	max = ULONG_MAX;
+	opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_floor(dev, &max);
+	if (IS_ERR(opp))
+		return PTR_ERR(opp);
+	dev_pm_opp_put(opp);
+	gov = dmc->rate == max ? DEVFREQ_GOV_PERFORMANCE
+			       : DEVFREQ_GOV_USERSPACE;
+	dev_info(dev, "DDR at %lu Hz from the loader, held there (%s)\n",
+		 dmc->rate, gov);
+
+	dmc->devfreq = devm_devfreq_add_device(dev, &dmc->profile, gov,
 					       &dmc->ondemand);
 	if (IS_ERR(dmc->devfreq))
 		return PTR_ERR(dmc->devfreq);
